<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila affinis Turing wavenumber at 2.4 µm (Holocene, detail tier) — MorphoEval overall 82.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrated Schnakenberg kinetics with Du chosen so the determinant-minimizing wavenumber is 2.444 µm at Dv/Du = 10. The fastest linear mode was 2.652 µm and the nonlinear FFT selected 2.619 µm (metrics-pass1.json). Pearson r between continuum and discrete growth rates was 0.9997 and the equal-diffusivity ablation stayed negative (sigma_max = -0.099). The habitus frame matches the CC BY-SA photograph; the 2.444 µm field is not resolved by that photograph's 250 µm scale bar. Weighted overall on the Pass-1 gap is 82.0. Calibration of Du onto the fastest mode is the Pass-2 fix. Overall 82.0/100 (faithfulness 80.1, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 2087759 B, 960×720 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7 (sha256 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7), spec_fingerprint 1d549b7322f4ffdb1233c8d9a23519c69dfd24ec8235a0131e1cb9b06ccb909d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1d549b7322f4ffdb1233c8d9a23519c69dfd24ec8235a0131e1cb9b06ccb909d; artifact_sha256: 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_affinis_specimen.jpg=83062d706a605b86..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9939928504f37754..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=368c8326ecee5c1b..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=2164e988b14e5446...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Sturtevant 1916 named Drosophila affinis. Miller 1955 described its sex combs. | Wittkopp, True and Carroll 2002: Yellow and Ebony place adult cuticular melanin. Shoup 1966 described melanogaster pigment-granule ontogeny.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, classical k_c, and a periodic Schnakenberg integration on a 48.88 µm by 36.66 µm patch. | Chronoseries comparison against the assigned berryi 98.43 µm (19 Ma) and americana 138.7 µm (0 Ma) wavelengths. | Du, Dv solved for lambda_c = 2.444 µm at diffusivity ratio 10. These are not the sibling slots' alpha_scale coefficients.; transfer_boundary: Shoup 1966 is D. melanogaster, not a measurement of D. affinis granule spacing. | The sex comb is the species diagnosis. Its tooth spacing is not this wavelength. | Berryi and americana are Delphi chronoseries neighbors, not a demonstrated ancestor-descendant pair.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a new electron-microscope measurement of D. affinis pigment granules. | Does not claim the habitus photograph resolves a 2.444 µm wave. The print scale bar is 250 µm. | Does not claim the Pass-1 nonlinear FFT (2.619 µm) equals the assigned scale.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Retune Du so the fastest-growing mode, which the nonlinear FFT follows, sits on 2.444 µm. Pass 1 left it at 2.652 µm (FFT 2.619 µm).",
        "remediation needed: R2: Redraw the chronoseries panel so the 2.444 µm bar is readable on a log axis next to 98.43 µm and 138.7 µm.",
        "remediation needed: R3: Report specimen-mask foreground, circularity, coherency, and the orientation-histogram KS against the habitus, with reference values that are not copies of the measurements.",
        "remediation needed: R4: Nanopub signing was not performed. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not on this machine.",
        "remediation needed: R5: One habitus photograph. The 250 µm scale bar does not resolve 2.444 µm, and there is no second assessor." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
